pocket-motion-only: TEX_QUAD_MIP and TEX_TRI_MIP are drawn by this software rasteriser alone, and every upstream backend parses the draw list by a closed op set; the PSP GE samples one bound texture with its own mip registers and a no_std EBOOT has no room for a second copy of every texture a third its size, the ESP32 and Symbian RGB565 hosts draw images at their own size, and a GPU backend asks its driver for a mip chain rather than reading one the core reduced.

0058 — `image-filter-trilinear`: an image drawn below its size reads a mip
chain the core reduced from its bytes, two levels picked by the drawn
footprint, each bilinear, blended. Nearest reads a few texels of the dozens
under a pixel and bilinear four, so an image drawn at 15% of its size lands
on whichever texels the grid happens to cross, and a slow push redraws it
differently at every frame: shimmer. `baselines/phase4-minification.md`
measured bilinear adequate to 2x and failing beyond it.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `engine/core/src/mip.rs` (new): `MipChain`, the levels below a texture's
  own. Level k + 1 is level k reduced to max(1, floor(w/2)) x
  max(1, floor(h/2)) by an exact area average — each output texel's span cut
  against each source texel's in units of 1/dst of a texel, so every weight is
  an integer and an odd side spreads three texels over two — of premultiplied
  texels, stored straight RGBA8888, in u64 sums rounded half up. Keyed by the
  texture's revision. `footprint` (texels per logical px along the screen
  axis that crosses the most: the longer column of the screen-to-texel
  Jacobian), `triangle_footprint`, and `pick`: r = rho / scale at or below
  one is the texture alone; above it the level is r's exponent and the
  blend weight the top eight bits of its mantissa, linear between powers of
  two and continuous across them, so no transcendental reaches a pixel.
- `engine/core/src/lib.rs`: `Texture.mips`, `Texture::ensure_mips`,
  `Ui::texture_mips`; `update_texture_t8` drops the levels of the bytes it
  overwrites. Every `Texture` literal starts with none.
- `engine/core/src/resources.rs`, `engine/wasm/src/lib.rs`:
  `RenderResources::texture_mips`, empty by default; the auxiliary resources
  pass the Ui's through.
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: an image node whose style carries
  `image-filter-trilinear` emits TEX_QUAD_MIP (axis-aligned) or TEX_TRI_MIP
  (turned, skewed, mirrored, or a cell of a perspective mesh) with its
  footprint, computed from the unrounded world transform — for a 3D cell the
  larger of its two triangles', from the projected corners before clipping
  and rounding. The chain is reduced there, when a footprint above one texel
  first needs it: a texture never drawn below its size costs nothing.
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: the two ops; `MipRead`, the two levels one op
  reads; TEX_QUAD_MIP tables its taps per column and per row for each level
  as 0021 does for one. At r <= 1 the read is the texture's own bilinear
  read, byte for byte, whatever the texture's flag.
- `engine/core/src/damage.rs`, `compositor.rs`, `lib.rs`: the ops' lengths
  (10 and 13 words) and bounds, which are TEX_QUAD's and TEX_TRI's.
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`, `contracts/spec/spec.ts` and the generated
  `spec.rs`, microts `spec.rs` and `component-types-microts.ts`: PROP
  `imageFilter` (221, enum ImageFilter { Texture, Trilinear }), DRAW_OP
  `texQuadMip` 72 and `texTriMip` 73. 221 because an open branch's colour
  filters and pixel origins hold 212-220, after the vector-path props'
  211; 72 is the next op after 0042's PATH. Numbered 0058 because open
  branches hold 0051-0057.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `image-filter-texture` (the default) and
  `image-filter-trilinear`; `tests/tailwind.test.ts` holds both and refuses
  any other filter word.
- Tests: `mip.rs` holds the reduction against an oracle that replicates
  every texel into a dst-sized block and box-averages, over nine sizes and
  four pixel formats; a transparent neighbour lending a level no colour;
  1000x1500 halving to 1x1 in ten levels at most a third of the base's bytes;
  a new revision reduced again; `pick`'s table and its continuity across
  every power of two. `raster.rs` holds TEX_QUAD_MIP and TEX_TRI_MIP at
  r <= 1 against TEX_QUAD and TEX_TRI of the same bytes uploaded linear;
  TEX_QUAD_MIP against a per-pixel trilinear reference over four textures,
  seven footprints, two scales; and a one-texel checkerboard at 6.9 texels a
  pixel, grey at every sub-texel shift where nearest and bilinear swing.
  `tests.rs` holds the footprint an image carries under six rotations, a
  squeeze, a sub-rect and a perspective turn, and the chain reduced only when
  a draw reads below the texture and again when its bytes change.

Red cases, each an edit to this patch, each turning the named test red and
no other: the alpha average rounded down, or an odd side reduced as a 2x2
box (`reduce_is_the_area_average_of_the_replicated_texture`); colour
averaged straight (`a_transparent_neighbour_lends_a_level_no_colour`);
halving rounded up (`a_chain_halves_to_one_texel_and_costs_at_most_a_third`);
a chain kept across revisions (`a_new_revision_is_reduced_again`); the weight
read from the wrong mantissa bits (`pick_reads_the_exponent_and_the_mantissa`);
level 0 read nearest, in the triangle's sampler or the quad's taps
(`a_mip_read_no_wider_than_a_texel_is_the_bilinear_read`); no level below the
base ever picked (`a_minified_checkerboard_reads_its_average_and_holds_still_as_it_moves`);
the coarse level dropped, read one level too deep, or its row tap taken from
the fine level (`tex_quad_mip_is_the_per_pixel_trilinear_read`); a rotation's
cross terms dropped, or the narrower axis taken
(`a_trilinear_image_carries_its_footprint_under_any_affine_world`); one
footprint for every cell of a perspective mesh
(`a_trilinear_image_in_perspective_carries_each_cells_footprint`); a chain
reduced for every trilinear draw
(`a_chain_is_reduced_when_a_draw_reads_below_the_texture_and_again_when_its_bytes_change`).

